                            <comment id="498298" author="adilger" created="Tue, 21 Jul 2026 21:24:56 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This may be a duplicate of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20308" title="sanity-lfsck test_0: el10.1: FAIL: (10) Expect nothing to be repaired, but got: 98" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20308"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20308&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20424" title="osd_fid_unpack() unexpected packed fid size: 0" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20424"&gt;LU-20424&lt;/a&gt; with a different symptom.  It is only failing this way on newer kernels (optional test sessions), and most of the time sanity-lfsck test_0 is failing with "&lt;tt&gt;Error:  '(10) Expect nothing to be repaired, but got: 97'&lt;/tt&gt;" and then all of the subtests fail until test_5 fails with "&lt;tt&gt;Fail to cleanup the env!&lt;/tt&gt;".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;About 7% of the 30% of test_5 failures are caused by this issue, but the lack of linkEA is similar to the missing dirdata in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20424" title="osd_fid_unpack() unexpected packed fid size: 0" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20424"&gt;LU-20424&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
